(Q/'COHORT-REVIEW.md').write_text('# FX18 restraint assembly review\n\nOriginal atlas 05 row 2 shows broken amber bands and diamond clasps, aligned open arcs, a closed double restraint, then a slightly tighter double restraint. The old RGB magenta atlas was used as identity evidence only. All selected sources are newly authored genuine RGBA.\n\n## Phase interpretation\n\n1. scattered-bands: four separate long arcs, two side clasps, five peripheral diamonds and one short lower-left band fragment; both center joints remain absent.\n2. aligning-ring: upper and lower arc halves join with central clasps. The left upper latch is near/contacting; other side gaps remain.\n3. closed-restraints: side joints close, the front arc lifts and a complete lower second band forms. Three central clasps and two side clasps remain readable.\n4. settled-restraints: both closed bands persist with an 11.2% narrower, 10.0% shorter main assembly. Side clasps tighten inward and detached diamonds settle.\n\n## Measurements and caveats\n\n'+ '\n'.join('- '+s for s in caveats)+'\n\n## Verification\n\nActual full-resolution black/white composites and colored overview, native32/64 on black, white, bright stone, green ground, dark earth and checker were inspected. Full1–2–3–4 and terminal3–4–1–2 comparisons were inspected. The terminal comparison is not a runtime loop. Parent accepted the corrected static quartet.\n\nFour equal1/12-second frames and one play are confirmed in14 canonical APNGs;14 separate slow repeating diagnostics are labeled. All112 decoded APNG frames exactly match the expected exports. Live browser/game playback remains unobserved.\n'.replace('an11','an 11').replace(',10',', 10').replace('native32','native 32').replace('Full1','Full 1').replace('terminal3','terminal 3').replace('equal1','equal 1').replace('in14','in 14').replace(';14','; 14').replace('All112','All 112'))
